1
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:06,720
He who hath bent him o'er the dead

2
00:00:06,720 --> 00:00:08,940
Ere the first day of Death is fled,

3
00:00:09,380 --> 00:00:10,920
The first dark day of Nothingness,

4
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:13,320
The last of Danger and Distress,

5
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:16,620
(Before Decay's effacing fingers

6
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:19,720
Have swept the lines where Beauty lingers,)

7
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:22,400
And marked the mild angelic air,

8
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:25,240
The rapture of Repose that's there,

9
00:00:25,740 --> 00:00:28,560
The fixed yet tender traits that streak

10
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:31,540
The languor of the placid cheek,

11
00:00:32,180 --> 00:00:34,660
And—but for that sad shrouded eye,

12
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:38,000
That fires not, wins not, weeps not, now,

13
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,880
And but for that chill, changeless brow,

14
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:44,480
Where cold Obstruction's apathy

15
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:46,900
Appals the gazing mourner's heart,

16
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:50,380
As if to him it could impart

17
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:53,020
The doom he dreads, yet dwells upon;

18
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:56,820
Yes, but for these and these alone,

19
00:00:56,820 --> 00:00:59,820
Some moments, aye, one treacherous hour,

20
00:01:00,120 --> 00:01:03,100
He still might doubt the Tyrant's power;

21
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:07,620
So fair, so calm, so softly sealed,

22
00:01:07,880 --> 00:01:10,560
The first, last look by Death revealed!

23
00:01:11,140 --> 00:01:13,300
Such is the aspect of this shore;

24
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:16,940
'Tis Greece, but living Greece no more!

